# The writable globals the tick may keep (tests/globals.sh). One line each:
# FILE:SYMBOL (extended regexes over the object's base name and the symbol)
# then the reason. Everything else the tick mutates lives in struct env
# (engine/env.h), a world, or the replay's per-dimension states.
#
# The environment itself
env:env_first                     the process's first environment, the storage every single-world tool ticks in
env:nw_env                        the current environment (thread-local): a harness points it at the one it ticks
env:nw_thread_scratch             the thread's own scratch (thread-local): a pool worker's, empty between calls (env.h struct env_scratch)
#
# Tables built once before main by a constructor and only read after, the
# same for every environment
activate:ids                      block, item and material ids by registry name
dig:ids                           block and item ids by registry name
harvest:ids                       block ids by registry name
harvestdrops:ids                  block and item ids by registry name
drops:(ITEM|BLOCK_ITEM)           Item.getItemFromBlock and the drop names' item ids
container:wood_index              Material.wood's index
decorator:leaves_i                Material.leaves' index
features_lakes:MAT_(AIR|LEAVES|LAVA|WATER)   material indices
features_nether:MAT_AIR           Material.air's index
features_springs:MAT_(AIR|LAVA|PORTAL|WATER) material indices
features_springs:SP_CLASS          func_149807_p and the liquid materials by id
fire:fire_air                     Material.air's index
pathfind:pf_mat_(air|lava)        material indices
populate_nether:MAT_LEAVES        Material.leaves' index
populate:PRECIP_STOP              the precipitation walk's stops by id
world:COLUMN_EMIT                 light sources by an id's low byte (func_150811_f's walk)
servertick:st_air_index           Material.air's index
ticks:mat_air                     Material.air's index
world:air_material_index          Material.air's index
world:TICK_RANDOMLY               Block.getTickRandomly by id
world:SET_PLAIN                   the blocks whose breakBlock and onBlockAdded are empty, by id
blockcb:bc_(mat_air|mat_water|mat_lava|mat_leaves)   material indices
blockcb:bc_rail                   the rail classes by block id
blockcb:bc_cls                    the classes the callbacks test, a bit each, by block id
(features_plants|features_trees_small|randomtick):MATI_(AIR|LEAVES|WATER)   material indices
features_lakes:TEMP_NOISE         BiomeGenBase's temperature Perlin noise, Random(1234)
particles_live:temp_noise         BiomeGenBase's temperature Perlin noise, Random(1234)
randomtick:flower_noise           BiomeGenBase.field_150606_ad, Random(2345)
randomtick:rt_diffuse             Block.field_149783_u (rt_light_diffuse) by block id
jmath:MH_SIN                      MathHelper.SIN_TABLE
living:(nether_)?light_brightness_table   WorldProvider.lightBrightnessTable, both providers
pathfind:pf_move_class            the path finder's block classes
spawning:(lists|jungle_creature|swamp_monster|mush_creature|empty_list|scattered_witch)   the biomes' spawn lists
gunzip:fixed_(lit|dist)           DEFLATE's fixed Huffman tables
gunzip:crc_fold_ok                the CPU's carry-less multiply support
sha1:blocks                       the SHA-1 block function the CPU supports
snapshot:pow_(lo|hi)              FNV-1a prime powers for the chunk hash
#
# Caches of pure functions, shared by every environment: a hit returns what a
# miss computes, whichever environment filled it. Not thread-safe; one thread
# per environment would need them per environment or locked.
[a-z_0-9]+:nbt_put_site_\.[0-9]+  nbt_put's per call site key: the literal's interned key (nbtjson.h)
[a-z_0-9]+:nbtw_site_\.[0-9]+  nbtw.h's per call site key, the same (NBTW_K)
living:attr_name_site  each attribute name's interned key, the same (living.c attr_instance_w)
nbtjson:key_(table|cap|count|cache|lock)   the interned keys and short strings: content-addressed, append-only, never freed; a miss takes the lock
itemtab:tabs(_lock)?                the HUD's item tables by scene (the renderer's, never the tick's): append-only, never freed; a miss takes the lock
rbshare:shares(_lock)?              the block renderer's tables by asset directory (the renderer's, never the tick's): append-only, never freed; a miss takes the lock
#
# Harness machinery, not game state
grave:.*                          the dead-living reclaimer (grave.h): a conservative scan of the process between rows
arena:live_arenas                 the arenas alive in the process, written when an environment is made or freed (the grave's scan reads their pools)
